      "title": "Chapter 12 — Reading the numbers",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The source highlights CPA, CPC, CTR, ROAS, purchase count, and ad-level performance. These metrics are useful when interpreted together.\nMetric\tMeaning\tWhat it helps answer\nSpend\tAmount spent on ads\tHow much budget has been used?\nImpressions\tNumber of ad displays\tIs the ad being delivered?\nCPM\tCost per 1,000 impressions\tHow expensive is reach?\nCTR\tClick-through rate\tDoes the creative motivate clicks?\nCPC\tCost per click\tHow much does each click cost?\nLanding-page views\tVisits that load the page\tAre clicks becoming real visits?\nAdd-to-cart rate\tAdd-to-cart events relative to visits\tDoes the offer create intent?\nCheckout initiation\tCustomers beginning checkout\tAre shoppers progressing?\nPurchase conversion rate\tPurchases relative to visits\tDoes the page and offer convert?\nCPA\tAd spend per purchase\tWhat does acquisition cost?\nAOV\tAverage order value\tHow much does an average order generate?\nROAS\tAttributed revenue divided by ad spend\tHow much revenue is attributed per ad dollar?\nContribution after ads\tRevenue less variable costs and ads\tIs the order economically viable?",
        "12.1 Diagnose the funnel\nLow CTR: The hook, audience relevance, creative, or offer may be weak. Review the first seconds and the message.",
        "Good CTR but few landing-page views: The page may load slowly, the click may be low quality, or tracking may be misconfigured.",
        "Landing-page views but few add-to-carts: The product page may not explain the value, price, or product details clearly.",
        "Add-to-carts but few purchases: Check shipping cost, delivery estimate, checkout friction, payment methods, trust, and unexpected fees.",
        "Purchases but negative contribution: The product economics, selling price, supplier cost, shipping, or CPA may be unsustainable.",
        "Metrics are diagnostic clues, not verdicts in isolation. Small sample sizes can fluctuate substantially.\n12.2 Understand the source's reported ad metrics\nThe source reports approximately:\n- $1,064 spend\n- 74 purchases\n- $14.38 CPA\n- $0.86 CPC\n- 4.94% CTR\n- 2.72 ROAS\nIt later reports a winning ad with 63 purchases at around $13 CPA. The operator says this ad carried much of the campaign and planned to make more variations of it.",
        "These figures can illustrate how a campaign report is read. They do not establish that the same CPA or ROAS is achievable for another product, country, account, or advertiser."
      ]
